USER     # `dispose --decided-at T` writes T into custody.json (`disposition.at`) and keeps the tool clock in the
USER     # line's `at` (INTERFACE 1; kit/custody_ledger.py). The value to compare with — and the value the record's
USER     # disposition.at gets — is the line's decided_at; a line with no decided_at (the base form) uses `at`.
